id: pm-db8onn
title: Auto Release blocker closure ignores successful recovery dispatch and reruns the stale tag-push workflow
description: "After v2026.8.5 was successfully recovered by workflow_dispatch run 31001951195, closing GitHub blocker #898 started Auto Release run 31002881238. Its same-day recovery query filtered Release runs to event=push and selected failed historical tag-push run 30994468126, ignoring the newer successful workflow_dispatch run. It reran the stale tag workflow, failed static quality on historical checkout state, and reopened a resolved blocker."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: "area:release",auto-release,exact-tag-recovery,github-actions,reliability,run-selection
created_at: "2026-08-05T11:59:56.790Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-15T10:20:23.079Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-15T10:20:22.359Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-15T10:20:22.359Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 360
acceptance_criteria: "Run selection considers both tag-push and guarded workflow_dispatch Release runs for the exact tag; a newer successful immutable recovery wins over an older failed push run; reruns execute the reviewed current workflow with exact-tag source selection rather than historical workflow code; executable contracts cover successful dispatch plus failed historical push, current-day retry markers, and issue close/reopen behavior; GitHub #898 closes after production proof without creating or moving another same-day tag"
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make blocker recovery select the authoritative successful exact-tag run
value: Resolved release incidents must remain resolved instead of spawning redundant expensive reruns and false blocker state
impact: "Prevents stale workflow execution, misleading open incidents, and wasted CI/review capacity after a successful immutable recovery"
outcome: Issue-closure retry logic uses an explicit authoritative run-selection contract across push and dispatch recovery events
why_now: "The production v2026.8.5 recovery succeeded, but the cleanup closure immediately reopened its blocker through stale run selection"
parent: pm-e70zh5
risk: high
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: GitHub Actions issue-closure Auto Release run 31002881238; successful Release recovery run 31001951195; tag-push Release run 30994468126; GitHub issue #898
repro_steps: "Successfully recover an existing daily tag through release.yml workflow_dispatch, then close the same-day Auto Release blocker. Observe auto-release.yml query only event=push, rerun the failed historical tag-push workflow, and reopen the blocker even though npm and GitHub Release are healthy."
resolution: "Auto Release now short-circuits same-day immutable tags before expensive preparation, selects SHA-bound successful push or default-branch dispatch evidence over stale failures, and dispatches the current reviewed Release workflow only when recovery evidence is absent."
expected_result: "Closing a resolved release blocker recognizes successful exact-tag publication, records the existing immutable release, and leaves the blocker closed without rerunning historical workflow code or creating a second daily release."
actual_result: "Production issues-event run 31878905982 selected existing successful Release run 31874087916 for v2026.8.15 at fbb7bd44d89d7d393b843e19f28dcb7f99367562 before analyzer/build work, emitted success receipts, kept GH #1017 closed, and preserved one tag, one release, and one npm version."
